{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q245825","formula":"F₃NS","hill":"F3NS","elements":["N","F","S"],"composition":{"F":3.0,"N":1.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Trifluoridonitridosulfur","ru":"Тиазилтрифторид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Thiazyl trifluoride is a chemical compound of nitrogen, sulfur, and fluorine, having the formula NSF3. It exists as a stable, colourless gas, and is an important precursor to other sulfur-nitrogen-fluorine compounds. It has tetrahedral molecular geometry around the sulfur atom, and is regarded to be a prime example of a compound that has a sulfur-nitrogen triple bond.","ru":"Тиазилтрифторид — химическое соединение, состоящее из азота, серы и фтора с химической формулой NSF3. Он представляет собой стабильный бесцветный газ и является важным предшественником других соединений серы, азота и фтора. Он имеет тетраэдрическую молекулярную геометрию вокруг атома серы и считается ярким примером соединения, имеющего тройную связь сера-азот."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":140008,"mass":103.07,"charge":0,"smiles":"N#S(F)(F)F","inchikey":"UQUPGRNSXINWBS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"azanylidyne(trifluoro)-lambda6-sulfane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"140008","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.042,"el":"S"},{"x":0.36,"y":1.443,"z":-0.481,"el":"F"},{"x":1.071,"y":-1.033,"z":-0.481,"el":"F"},{"x":-1.429,"y":-0.41,"z":-0.483,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.001,"y":0.0,"z":1.403,"el":"N"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[0,3,1],[0,4,3]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q245825","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiazyl_trifluoride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/